  "summary": "San Jose Police Chief Paul Joseph publicly defended his March claim that ALPR data had not been misused, despite SJPD investigating an officer at the time for sharing Flock ALPR location data with a family member who used it to track a domestic violence accuser. Joseph said his March answer referred narrowly to unauthorized access by outside agencies and immigration enforcement, and that he couldn't disclose the ongoing personnel investigation; civil rights advocates called the explanation insufficient. The council is advancing a second round of safeguard proposals including limits on personal-device access and a shortened 30-day retention window.",
  "key_quotes": [
